      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=4{x}^{2}-16x+5.$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=4$ and $b=-16$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{(-16)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{8} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=2.$",
